      "text": "What HULI-KAMOTE is, in one minute",
      "kicker": "The project"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "b",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "HULI-KAMOTE"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is a thesis project of the College of Computing Studies in Zamboanga City: a computer-vision system that finds traffic violations in video, so officers can review them without standing at the roadside. "
        },
        {
          "type": "i",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Huli"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " means 'caught'; "
        },
        {
          "type": "i",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "kamote"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is slang for a reckless driver. It finds vehicles with a "
        },
        {
          "type": "term",
          "key": "YOLO",
          "shown": "YOLO"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " detector, follows each one with a tracker ("
        },
        {
          "type": "term",
          "key": "DeepSORT",
          "shown": "DeepSORT"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "), reads licence plates ("
        },
        {
          "type": "term",
          "key": "OCR",
          "shown": "OCR"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "), and then decides each violation with a small, explainable rule. A person always reviews what the system flags."
        }
      ],
      "is_note": false
    },
